{"name":"Peaslake","hex":"#8caa95","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Peaslake","blocks":[{"text":"Peaslake, Hoe and Colman's Hill are in the centre of the Surrey Hills National Landscape and mid-west of the Greensand Ridge about 5 miles (8.0 km) ESE of Guildford. Surrounded by denser pine and other coniferous forest-clad hills, the three conjoined settlements have a small core in Peaslake itself with the amenities of a village, but are otherwise lightly scattered settlements at a higher elevation than the centre of Shere, the civil parish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Peaslake%2C_Village_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_108979.jpg/330px-Peaslake%2C_Village_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_108979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peaslake","wikidata":"Q7158452"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/St_Mark%2C_Peaslake%2C_Surrey_-_Window_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1653151.jpg/330px-St_Mark%2C_Peaslake%2C_Surrey_-_Window_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1653151.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/St_Mark%2C_Peaslake%2C_Surrey_-_Window_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1653151.jpg/330px-St_Mark%2C_Peaslake%2C_Surrey_-_Window_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1653151.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt_Mark%2C_Peaslake%2C_Surrey_-_Window_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1653151.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Path_through_the_Hurt_Wood_-_geograph.org.uk_-_46538.jpg/500px-Path_through_the_Hurt_Wood_-_geograph.org.uk_-_46538.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Path_through_the_Hurt_Wood_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465